 ## Belum Diimplementasikan
 
 API delete bukan bagian dari repositori ini.
+
+## Hasil INSERT tanpa pengisian generated ID
+
+```go
+result, err := tx.CreateWith(&assignment).ExecResult()
+if err != nil {
+    return err
+}
+rows, err := result.RowsAffected()
+```
+
+ExecResult memakai mapper, dialect builder dan SQL/args yang sama dengan
+CreateWith(...).DryRun() tanpa returning (Mode=exec). Hasil eksekusi dan error
+diteruskan ke caller; method tidak membaca LastInsertId, mengisi primary key,
+atau melakukan commit/rollback. Caller memutuskan makna count nol/lebih dari
+satu dan error RowsAffected. WithReturning ditolak sebelum eksekusi.
+Create, Exec, Scan, ScanInto dan DryRun existing tetap kompatibel. Gunakan model
+khusus INSERT untuk mempertahankan default kolom yang tidak disertakan; nilai
+nol dan nullable mengikuti aturan mapper existing.
diff --git a/docs/create-update.md b/docs/create-update.md
index acdc1f3..8e0aaf9 100644
--- a/docs/create-update.md
+++ b/docs/create-update.md
@@ -251,3 +251,22 @@ adapter also exposes `DryRunUpdateBulk`.
 ## Not Implemented
 
 Delete APIs are not part of this repository.
+
+## Insert result without generated ID
+
+```go
+result, err := tx.CreateWith(&assignment).ExecResult()
+if err != nil {
+    return err
+}
+rows, err := result.RowsAffected()
+```
+
+`ExecResult` uses the same mapper, dialect builder and SQL/args as
+`tx.CreateWith(&assignment).DryRun()` without returning intent (`Mode=exec`).
+It returns the execution result/error and does not read LastInsertId, assign a
+primary key, or finalize the transaction. Callers decide whether zero/multiple
+rows or a RowsAffected error are acceptable. WithReturning is rejected before
+execution. Existing Create, Exec, Scan, ScanInto and DryRun keep their behavior.
+Use an insert-specific model to preserve omitted database defaults; explicit
+zero values and nullable fields follow the existing mapper rules.
diff --git a/docs/query-builder.id.md b/docs/query-builder.id.md
index a438e7d..704c87f 100644
--- a/docs/query-builder.id.md
+++ b/docs/query-builder.id.md
@@ -180,3 +180,39 @@ err := db.UseModel(User{}).
     Where("email = ?", email).
     First(&user)
 ```
+
+## Komposisi subquery
+
+Susun child builder melalui transaction yang sama. Child disimpan sebagai
+snapshot: perubahan builder asal sesudah komposisi tidak mengubah parent.
+Dialect, placeholder, identifier quoting dan urutan argument mengikuti parent,
+termasuk offset setelah nilai SET pada UPDATE. Child nil/invalid atau alias
+invalid menghasilkan error sebelum eksekusi. Alias derived table harus berupa
+identifier sederhana dan tidak memakai AS.
+
+```go
+eligible := tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id").Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE")
+
+q := tx.UseModel(User{}).
+    WhereExists(tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+        Select("user_id").Where("user_id = users.id").Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE"))
+
+q = q.WhereInQuery("users.id", eligible)
+q = q.WhereNotExists(tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id").Where("user_id = users.id").Where("status = ?", "REVOKED"))
+
+names := tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id", "MIN(role_name) AS first_name").
+    Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE").GroupBy("user_id")
+q = q.LeftJoinQuery(names, "role_names", "role_names.user_id = users.id")
+
+preview, err := q.DryRun()
+count, err := q.DryRunCount()
+```
+
+DryRun, count dan pagination tidak mengubah builder asal. WhereExists,
+WhereNotExists dan WhereInQuery juga tersedia pada Updates/DryRunUpdates.
+Column, projection, correlation dan ON tetap berupa expression tepercaya seperti
+Where existing; whitelist identifier dan bind nilai request sebagai argument.
+Caller tidak perlu menulis SELECT utuh atau mengganti placeholder sendiri.
diff --git a/docs/query-builder.md b/docs/query-builder.md
index fbc7f5c..222f1e1 100644
--- a/docs/query-builder.md
+++ b/docs/query-builder.md
@@ -180,3 +180,38 @@ err := db.UseModel(User{}).
     Where("email = ?", email).
     First(&user)
 ```
+
+## Composable subqueries
+
+Compose child builders on the same transaction. Children are snapshots: later
+builder edits do not change a previously composed parent. Rendering uses the
+parent dialect, placeholder mode and identifier configuration, including nested
+arguments after UPDATE SET values. A nil/invalid child or invalid derived alias
+fails before execution. Derived aliases use a simple identifier without AS.
+
+```go
+eligible := tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id").Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE")
+
+q := tx.UseModel(User{}).
+    WhereExists(tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+        Select("user_id").Where("user_id = users.id").Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE"))
+
+q = q.WhereInQuery("users.id", eligible)
+q = q.WhereNotExists(tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id").Where("user_id = users.id").Where("status = ?", "REVOKED"))
+
+names := tx.UseModel(UserRole{}).
+    Select("user_id", "MIN(role_name) AS first_name").
+    Where("status = ?", "ACTIVE").GroupBy("user_id")
+q = q.LeftJoinQuery(names, "role_names", "role_names.user_id = users.id")
+
+preview, err := q.DryRun()
+count, err := q.DryRunCount()
+```
+
+`DryRun`, count and pagination preserve child/parent builders. `WhereExists`,
+`WhereNotExists` and `WhereInQuery` also work with `Updates` and `DryRunUpdates`.
+Expressions (columns, projections, correlations and ON) remain trusted SQL
+structure; bind request values and whitelist identifiers as with existing Where.
+Neither a complete SELECT string nor placeholder rewriting is needed in callers.
